WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 2 Student Video
Unit 1, Lesson 2: Faith

1
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.860
In college, I had a chance to be a resident assistant, a rep in charge of fun

2
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.300
activities and events on a floor.

3
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.340
Well, to help us have some compassion and understanding for students on our floor

4
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:24.460
who might have handicaps, the leadership decided that we would go around for a day

5
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.200
with a handicap of sorts. And my handicap was to wear a blindfold.

6
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.140
It really dawned on me for the first time since I had to go to the cafeteria, I had

7
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:39.160
to go to class with this blindfold on, how tough it is to navigate life without

8
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.660
sight. Well, how did I cope? How did I make it through the day?

9
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.920
Well, I had to ask somebody to help me.

10
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.200
Who did I ask? I didn't ask a stranger.

11
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.160
I didn't ask somebody I just met.

12
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.720
I asked somebody I trusted, one of my basketball teammates, to help me out through

13
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.720
the day. People often have the idea that faith is blind.

14
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.940
And when it comes to issues of religion, it's like we're frolicking around in the

15
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.700
dark and basing our beliefs on sheer ignorance.

16
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.900
Well this might be true for some religions but it is not true for Christianity.

17
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:19.260
You see biblically faith is trusting what we have reason to believe is

18
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:25.220
true. Just as I followed the guidance of my friend whom I had good reason to

19
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:30.820
trust when I was blindfolded. God asks us to follow Him, and He's given us good

20
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.840
reasons to trust Him.

21
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.570
We are not called to blind faith.

22
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.490
We see a remarkable pattern in Exodus chapter 7 through 14.

23
00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:56.250
God would do a powerful miracle through Moses, a sign which gave the people

24
00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:02.170
knowledge of who God is. And as a result, He called them to believe in Him and

25
00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:06.410
to place their trust in Him. So here's the pattern.

26
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.930
God would do a miracle through Moses.

27
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:13.230
This gave the people knowledge, and then they were called to belief.

28
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.710
Miracle, knowledge, belief. Consider an example.

29
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:23.630
In Exodus chapter 7 verse 17, Moses is about to do the miracle of turning the water,

30
00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:29.550
the Nile, into blood. And it says, by this you shall know.

31
00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:35.030
Now what is this? This is the miracle Moses was about to do.

32
00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:40.370
and it says and you shall know because that miracle would give them knowledge

33
00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:45.830
so Moses is doing this powerful miracle it gives them knowledge that the God of

34
00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:51.730
Israel is the one true God and then they're called to belief so our pattern which is

35
00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:56.270
clearly emerging is miracle knowledge and then belief

36
00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:02.270
we see the same pattern in the New Testament in the Gospel of Mark Jesus

37
00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.030
is in Capernaum and he's preaching in a home.

38
00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:08.690
And four men bring a paralytic to him.

39
00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:13.330
And they can't get into him, so they go up on the roof, remove the roof, and lower

40
00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:19.230
this paralytic down to Jesus. And Jesus sees them as a result of their faith, says,

41
00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:24.530
Son, your sins are forgiven. Now the scribes and Pharisees are thinking, wait a

42
00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.510
minute, who can forgive sins but God alone?

43
00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.390
This is blasphemy. What does Jesus do?

44
00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:32.090
If you skip down and look at verse 10, it says this.

45
00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:37.890
Jesus said so that you may know that the Son of Man has

46
00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:43.630
authority on earth to forgive sins he looked at the paralytic he says rise pick up

47
00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:49.510
your mat and go home Jesus did that sign as proof that gave

48
00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.710
them knowledge of who he was and the implication was Jesus is the Son of God now

49
00:03:54.710 --> 00:04:00.590
believe in him you might be thinking wait a minute, didn't Jesus do the

50
00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.410
miracle because of the man's faith?

51
00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:09.670
After all, it says in Mark chapter 2 that Jesus, seeing their faith pronounced to

52
00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.290
the man, son, your sins are forgiven.

53
00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:17.930
Now it is true that God often does reward our faith by performing miracles.

54
00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.970
But let's ask a more basic question.

55
00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:24.970
Why did these four men and the paralytic come to Jesus in the first place?

56
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:29.790
And the answer is because, as Mark 1 tells us, Jesus had already been performing

57
00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.770
miracles. Jesus had already been casting out demons.

58
00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.870
He had given them evidence and signs that he's the Son of God.

59
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:42.190
So they came to him with confidence and put a faith in him that was well placed.

60
00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.590
Jesus calls people to love God with their heart, with their soul, with their

61
00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:52.490
strength, and with their minds. In the Old Testament, God says through the prophet

62
00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.830
Isaiah, come let us reason together.

63
00:04:56.310 --> 00:05:01.070
In the Old Testament and in the New Testament, God calls people to an intelligent

64
00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.490
faith and he still does the same today.

65
00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:10.070
This is why in the Gospel of John, a gospel which is written recording the miracles

66
00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:14.890
of Jesus and inviting people to a confident faith.

67
00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:20.770
At the very end of the Gospel, John writes in chapter 20 verses 30 through 31

68
00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:26.750
that Jesus has performed many other miracles not even recorded in this book.

69
00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:32.210
But they've been recorded so we might have confidence that Jesus is the Son of God,

70
00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:37.190
He's the Christ, and by believing in Him we may experience eternal life.

71
00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:43.370
The Gospel of John is written so we understand who Jesus is based on the miracles

72
00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:49.090
so we can have a confident faith and by having that faith experience eternal life.

73
00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:55.150
Biblical faith is not blind. The Bible invites non-believers to

74
00:05:55.150 --> 00:06:00.690
investigate the evidence, to consider the claims of Christ, and then to

75
00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:05.810
consider believing in Him. And as Christians, we're also not called to a blind

76
00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:11.050
faith. We are called to think deeply about our faith, to know why we believe what we

77
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:16.810
believe. We are called to have an answer when people ask us the reason for the hope

78
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.070
we have within.

